      "path": "src/Resilience/RetryPolicy.php",
      "reason": "Semgrep 1.155.0 cannot parse this file at all, so no rule examines it. Its PHP frontend rejects the `readonly` class modifier; on 744 other files it recovers and still scans the body, but here recovery fails at the `#[Api(since: '1.0.0')]` attribute on line 26 and the whole file is abandoned. Confirmed by planting `hash('sha256', 'PLANTED')` in a copy at line 132: forbidden-sha256 did not report it. What the hole hides: this file is not covered by forbidden-sha256 or export-fetchall-forbidden. It contains no hash call and no statement execution today, and the ADR-0006 broken-digest clause is enforced over it by Pulsar\\PHPStan\\Rules\\ForbidBrokenHashRule, which parses with PHP's own tokenizer and has no such blind spot. Accepted rather than worked around: rewriting framework source to suit a third-party parser puts the tool in charge of the code."
